<title>UK: World alumina output rose in 1996 - IPAI.</title>
<headline>World alumina output rose in 1996 - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>World production of alumina in 1996 rose to 40.841 million tonnes from 38.457 million in 1995, latest International Primary Aluminium Institute data showed.</p>
<p>In the final quarter of 1996 output was 10.155 million tonnes against 10.178 million in the third quarter and 9.730 million in last quarter 1995.</p>
<p>The IPAI said that with effect from first quarter 1997 its alumina production data will for the first time include input from China, Kazakhstan and Montenegro.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
